 echoing in his head and yet he was  forced to holster that power for what he  was told was for the betterment of the  universe i'm a big fan of this character  and with this particular piece of  artwork we had to adjust the original  pain's composition typically when  adapting manga to an anime format as you  saw in the last piece you have to make  alterations for it to fit within a 16x9  aspect ratio this all comes down to  framing and compositional awareness the  first goku piece at the beginning of the  video was initially a test to see if  this would actually work as a concept  for a video so little thought was put  into changing it up for tv in this  particular case we altered the original  by playing around with the position of  the incoming fist and added smears and  speed effect lines for the punch to  better match how it would look in  animation the result looks promising but  in reality we won't know how good it  looks until we apply mix's filter  and there we have it as authentic as  ever let this serve as perhaps an  indication of how this character might  be depicted once it makes it to our  screens one day in the future next up  yours truly  the beauty of converting styles for the  purposes of a video like this is that we  get to effectively work as animation  supervisors the staff members on an  episode in charge of ensuring drawings  are anatomically sound and on model in  the same way they do we're often drawing  over someone else's artwork keeping what  works and changing other aspects and  shapes contained within the drawing to  bring it more in line with what we  expect from the shintani design sheets  honestly as artists it feels a bit weird  with our views on tracing but this is  how it's done in the industry so we're  following suit in other words if we're  lucky in the bass drawing is solid we  can just change the shapes and feature  placement a little and call it a day but  in some instances we run into minor  anatomical issues that require our  addressing and this is often part of the  adaptation process and so due to this  reality when it came to converting this  piece into shintani's style i not only  had to change the style itself but i  ended up having to redraw the  foundational drawing of that one arm and  that was just the first struggle many of  these new characters only have their  official colors revealed via the full  color manga which uses very saturated  colors that just don't look anything  like the color design seen in modern  dragon ball content and so our solution  was this use the manga colors as a  reference and then find and adjust  existing colors in broly to match them  best unfortunately for me i referenced  this image for how to color him and that  image happens to be one of the only  instances where 73 is colored  incorrectly there's actually a mistake  on his chest thankfully though this  mistake was caught before we finalized  the images just gotta throw it through  the filter now and  there you have it the arm is fixed the  style is shifted and the color is  accurate very happy with the way this  one turned out  next up  editor-san the female trio from the  galactic bandit brigade don't play a  major part in the morrow arc but their  battle against rosh is a fun one and  tackling more aggressive looking girls  with a shintani twist seem like an  interesting idea so here we are editor  stan sure had his work cut out for him  with this one not only did he have three  characters to rework but their fairly  detailed designs and trying to refine  them into something suitable for  animation is no easy feat following the  aforementioned philosophy of less is  more he cut back on the excessive lines  in the hair and let the shading do the  talking not too much however for a  couple of reasons the first is that this  is largely a comedic fight centered  around roshi's pervy antics but secondly  because even in serious situations  characters like chile never ended up  with quite as much of an extreme shading  increase so it was important to reflect  that reality here something he also  noticed immediately was that the center  girl was well she was missing a neck in  the original panel toyotaro was clearly  after an aggressive hunch shoulders look  but didn't quite nail it additionally to  better frame the panel in 16x9 editor  sand twisted her torso around allowing  for a more dynamic and balanced pose  with the rest of the team and most  importantly he restored the poor girl's  neck personally i think the best  addition he made was in varying up the  facial expressions to give each  individual character their own  distinctive personality admittedly it's  a slightly liberal take but one that i  think looks convincing and fitting and  with a little tlc from trev on the  eyebrows and shading it's ready for mix  to step in  beautifully blended in with those  distinctive inky lines and lovely  ambient lighting and you'd be forgiven  for thinking that this was right out of  an existing episode  nice job everyone and next up me  in reality shintani's design philosophy  is quite different from toyotaro's and  it has to be animation and illustration  are two very different mediums manga is  made up of stills so you can be as  detailed as you'd like but animation has  thousands of different drawings per  episode and they all need to be  consistent from one to another therein  lies the real challenge when adapting  from manga to anime designs one of the  major major shortcomings of yamamuro's  designs for super was how difficult they  were to animate rigid shapes with a  large number of lines do not make for a  forgiving design while super's crumbling  schedule brought about most of its  animation issues the designs for the  series certainly didn't do it any favors  this is the exact opposite of what  shintani's designs offered when he  overhauled the designs for the series  going into broly and so i had to keep  that in mind for my piece gas and alex  faces were pretty straightforward all i  had to do for ellick was to reference  goku's character sheets to form an  approximation of his face while gas on  the other hand was a little more  difficult fortunately though for me he  resembles kid buu and he pops up for  about a split second in the broly movie  giving me an easy reference okay two  faces done the clothes and hair however  were a whole other story in the manga  they're filled with complex lines that  just wouldn't work from an animation  standpoint but also turn into an  unreadable mess once mix's line filter  was applied in response to this i  reduced the number of lines and fell  back on simple shading instead to add  detail and depth and i think it worked  out pretty well to bring it all together  i grabbed the colors from whis's broly  movie character design and there you  have it all we gotta do now is apply the  filter and  those are some blue boys and might i add  that i love the crazy flare effects used  in this instance too if you're familiar  with magumi ishitani's work on dragon  ball super in one piece you'll know she  loves a good lens flare move out of the  way jj abrams very cinematic and  convincing but next up is me again  looking on as his surrogate's son makes  perhaps the biggest mistake of his life  comes this panel of mineto truth be told  i don't draw namekians very much and  i've never drawn an old one as far as i  can remember and so going into this  coupled with a strange angle and billowy  cloak i was certain this would be a  nightmare to fully realize but in  reality it ended up being the easiest of  my drawing surprisingly monito is  originally a toriyama design and seeing  as shintani didn't seem to do a whole  lot to change toriyama's stuff in broly  i tried to create a hybrid of toyotaro's  final version and toriyama's initial  version for the character both toyotaro  and toriyama have pretty different  approaches so this meant i needed my  interpretation to be more of a hybrid  meaning more regular proportions like  toyotaro but with rounder shapes like  toriyama the only real challenge i came  across was in finding an official color  palette for monito as a character and as  of writing this video the color manga  still hasn't arrived at his introduction  to the series yet however aj did manage  to find me the perfect and perhaps only  colored image of this character by  toyotaro at this point outside of that  everything was just cleaning up on the  details big blobby shapes on the cloak  for shading and now it's time for mix's  filter  i'm very happy with how this one turned  out very convincing and now moving on to  my last drawing next up is me of all the  pieces i've worked on in this video this  drawing here was the biggest struggle  not just because of the compositing  issues it later presented us with but  also because of the anatomical  abnormalities it continued to yield the  more i worked on it as i touched on  before during my drawing of 7-3  corrections to certain poses and manga  panels are a pretty standard affair when  adapting for the screen while i  absolutely see what toyotara was going  for in this piece when i started to lay  down the underlying anatomy to work on  this style shift i realized that not  only was the neck in the wrong place but  so too was the foremost arm itself and  when the shoulders arms and head are the  most important aspects of this piece  there ended up being very little i could  keep outside of the back and opposing  arm but in the end with a lot of trial  and error i managed to finish on  something i wasn't too unhappy with  facially it took a while to get things  right but thanks to the numerous  shintani illustrations out there i think  i managed to land on something pretty  convincing compositing was a big concern  with this one however auras and dragon  ball go pretty much hand in hand but in  super they became so blown out that it  honestly made it difficult to see the  underlying artwork while these  computer-generated auras were present in  broly also they were by design  significantly more readable particularly  when compared with super's counterparts  and so finding the effects and proper  balance to yield an authentic result was  quite tough but in the end once we  applied the final filter the results i  think speak for themselves this was a  struggle but it was worth it  next up with the final drawing of this  video  is trev  i absolutely adore granola's character  design in the manga there's a sort of  western gunslinger vibe he comes  packaged with and we wanted to preserve  that aspect of this persona here when we  selected this shot to create our own  approximation for an anime counterpart  with this one the biggest issues we face  came from our struggle to source an  appropriate backdrop to this one time  panel in the end we settled on this  hallway shot from frieza's ship in broly  trev also approached a large variety of  different shading styles and angles to  find what best suited partially drawing  from takahashi's section in the broly  movie in the end we went with something  quite striking and dramatic considering  the light is emanating from his  fingertips now something that did get a  little out of hand while super was on  the air was this notion that highlights  on characters equal bad when it comes to  dragon ball's anime however in reality  that is completely untrue highlights  aren't evil misuse of them is and boy  have they been misused over the years  but in the case of this image here that  trev is working on it makes complete  sense to use them due to it being highly  lit and this isn't a case of us picking  or choosing favorites either by the way  if we wind the clocks back and look at  dragon ball z you'll find them there  where appropriate too and even more  recently within the broly movie in the  end it's all how you choose to apply  them dragon ball super reached a point  where their presence made everyone look  like they were coated in oil with super  dragon ball heroes using it as a means  of showing health basically and in short  if used correctly this can be used to  tremendous effect to heighten the drama  of a particular scene and so while  keeping all of that in mind let's see  how this looks after we apply the filter  here you can see that mix has decided to  add his own changes like adding blur  around the edges to bring his face and  fingertips more into focus and that  coupled with the diffused lighting and  trev's incredible illustrative ability  make for i think magnificently  stupendous results  looking back at this video i was  incredibly blown away by the final  pieces on display i have an amazing team  one that without a video like this would  have been simply impossible to create in  the description as always you'll find a  list of all their social media accounts  and for the purposes of this video  specifically i'd like to shout out  mixtuskela on twitter for his incredible  knowledge and proficiency with that line  filter tool reminiscent of broly's art  design we couldn't have done it without  you fair warning though is twitter's a  little not safe for work so tread  carefully my friends but with that said  i can't wait to see what the future  holds for dragon ball i can't wait to  see if we end up being close with our  approximations of these shots but more  than anything else i hope you enjoyed  the video i'll see you all next week and  thank you so much for watching  [Music]  hmm  [Music]
 

